---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page title="Resume - Josh Symonds">
  <div class="resume">
    <header class="resume-header">
      <h1>Josh Symonds</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Builds agent platforms engineering orgs run on, and proves they pay for themselves.</p>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <a class="pill" href="mailto:josh@joshsymonds.com">josh@joshsymonds.com</a>
        <span class="pill">+1-773-480-4810</span>
        <a class="pill" href="https://github.com/joshsymonds">github.com/joshsymonds</a>
        <a class="pill pill-download" href="/joshsymonds_resume.pdf">Download PDF</a>
      </div>
      <p class="summary">Hands-on engineering leader with fifteen years of infrastructure and security engineering, now aimed at making coding agents reliable, cheap, and adopted.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Experience</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>Attain</h3>
          <span class="location">Remote &mdash; Santa Barbara, CA</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Director of SRE, Consumer Product</span>
          <span class="tenure">Mar 2026 &ndash; Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Marvin:</strong> Built and operate Marvin, a company-wide agent platform for code review, incident investigation, and internal workflows: 116 users across engineering, support, and operations in five months, about 50 weekly active.</li>
          <li><strong>Orchestration:</strong> Engineered the Go/Kubernetes orchestration: ephemeral agent workers on a Nix-built image, per-user OAuth tool credentials, immutable versioned model routes with live provider preflight and pointer-flip rollback.</li>
          <li><strong>Code Review:</strong> Shipped multi-stage agentic code review with independent verification and materiality filtering, posting inline GitLab comments: 2,100+ reviews, 87% positive on 300+ explicit ratings.</li>
          <li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Built a production-replay evaluation harness with frozen dev/holdout cases and a version-pinned LLM judge. Blind adjudication showed the incumbent verifier wrong on 37% of disputed verdicts; migrated review to open-weight models, cutting average cost per review 16&times; month over month while median wall time halved.</li>
          <li><strong>Incident Investigation:</strong> Automated investigation of 2,170+ alert threads, gathering evidence through kubectl, BigQuery, and logs before posting assessments or escalating. Validated through continuous synthetic canaries and blackbox acceptance tests against a fresh cluster per run.</li>
          <li><strong>Agent-Ready Monorepo:</strong> Built the layered documentation, agent skill framework, and progressive context disclosure that make a large fintech monorepo work under coding agents, shared by Marvin and engineers&rsquo; local Claude Code sessions.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>CrossnoKaye</h3>
          <span class="location">Santa Barbara, CA</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Senior Manager, Core Services / Principal Infrastructure Engineer</span>
          <span class="tenure">Jan 2021 &ndash; Feb 2026</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Go Services &amp; Tooling:</strong> Built production Go services and developer tools used daily across a 30+ microservice platform: Kubernetes service proxy, end-to-end testing framework, unified CLI.</li>
          <li><strong>Edge &amp; Platform:</strong> Built OS-level provisioning for industrial IoT edge agents and led the migration from k3os to Talos Linux; architected multi-cluster EKS with Flux CD, environment promotion, and rollback.</li>
          <li><strong>Org:</strong> Established the Core Services function; ran weekly LLM workshops that moved the engineering org onto AI tooling.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>Capital Markets Gateway</h3>
          <span class="location">Chicago, IL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Senior DevOps Engineer &amp; CISO</span>
          <span class="tenure">Oct 2019 &ndash; Dec 2020</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Platform &amp; Security:</strong> Built Kubernetes operators, multi-region failover, and custom Terraform providers; designed NIST CSF and ISO 27001 programs and passed audits by major financial institutions.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>M1 Finance</h3>
          <span class="location">Chicago, IL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">Chief Information Security Officer</span>
          <span class="tenure">Aug 2015 &ndash; Oct 2019</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Zero to Scale:</strong> Built greenfield AWS infrastructure that scaled M1 from zero to over a million customers; owned deployment pipelines and the security program; operated bare-metal Kubernetes and led the migration to EKS.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Selected Independent Engineering</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3><a href="https://savecraft.gg">Savecraft</a></h3>
          <span class="location">Go, TypeScript, Rust, WebAssembly, MCP</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Built and shipped an AI gaming companion spanning 14 games: open-source Go client with sandboxed WASM parsers, installer, and self-updater; hosted MCP tools authenticated through OAuth 2.1. Raw saves stay local; assistants receive structured game state and domain tools.</li>
          <li>Shipped a Go service pooling warm LuaJIT processes so agents can test build changes against <a href="/blog/path-of-building-doesnt-fit/">Path of Building&rsquo;s calculation engine</a>. Ported its perturbation algorithms to Go; measured 40 ms p50 / about 300 ms p99 swap-and-recompute latency with an eight-process pool.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3><a href="https://github.com/joshsymonds/gambit">Gambit</a> &amp; Tiltyard</h3>
          <span class="location">Claude Code, Pi, Go</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Released Gambit, a contract-to-release coding-agent plugin with isolated workspaces, owned-file boundaries, failure-signature model routing, and evidence-backed gates. Built Tiltyard to replay repository-derived implementation tasks against model and harness combinations, scoring correctness, reliability, quality, discipline, and cost.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3><a href="https://github.com/joshsymonds/nix-config">nix-config</a></h3>
          <span class="location">Nix &middot; 836 stars, 118 forks</span>
        </div>
        <p class="project-desc">NixOS and Home Manager configuration for a nine-host fleet.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Education</h2>

      <article class="job">
        <div class="job-header">
          <h3>University of Chicago</h3>
          <span class="location">Chicago, IL</span>
        </div>
        <div class="job-meta">
          <span class="title">BA in East Asian Languages and Civilizations</span>
          <span class="tenure">2001 &ndash; 2005</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <p class="pdf-link">
      <a href="/joshsymonds_resume.pdf">Download PDF version</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>

<style>
  .resume {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .resume-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .resume-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--black);
  }

  .contact-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    border: 2px solid var(--black);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    transition: box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  a.pill:hover {
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--black);
  }

  .pill-download {
    background: var(--coral);
    color: white;
    border: 2px solid var(--black);
  }

  .pill-download:hover {
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--black);
  }

  .tagline {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .summary {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: var(--space-md) auto 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .section h2 {
    color: var(--teal);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--black);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .section h2::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    right: -1.5rem;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%) rotate(45deg);
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--yellow);
    border: 2px solid var(--black);
  }

  .job {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .job-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .job-header h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    color: var(--teal);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .job-header h3::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: -1rem;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--coral);
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--black);
  }

  .location {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .job-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .job-meta .title {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .tenure {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }

  .project-desc {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .job ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .job ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .job ul li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--teal);
  }

  .pdf-link {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .pdf-link a {
    color: var(--coral);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    font-weight: 700;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .pdf-link a:hover {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .pdf-link a::after {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: var(--pink);
    border-radius: 50%;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
    vertical-align: middle;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--black);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .resume {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }

    .job-header, .job-meta {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.125rem;
    }

    .contact-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .pill {
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
